\ An uncaught parse failure inside a task must carry its diagnostic across the task boundary.
\
\ The task boundary builds its error object from the context's thrown error or execution details.
\ A parse failure left neither behind, so the scope reported `task failed without error details`
\ and the message the parser had already computed was lost.

boom: parse-time [ f "parse-time word failed" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;

[
  [ "boom" eval-string ] spawn drop
] task-scope
